---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="What's My Study Type? Free Quiz for Students, 8 Questions"
  description="What's my study type? Free quiz for students: 8 questions, under a minute, no sign-up — and you'll know exactly where you're losing time when you study."
  breadcrumbs={[
    { label: 'Tools', href: '/tools/' },
    { label: 'Study Type Quiz', href: '/en/tools/lerntyp-test/' },
  ]}
  lang="en"
  altHref="/tools/lerntyp-test/"
  wide
>
  <div class="wrap lt-page">
    <div class="lt-shell">
      <!-- ---------------------------------------------------- Intro -- -->
      <section id="s-intro" class="lt-screen on">
        <!-- 1 — Hook: the felt problem, not the product -->
        <div class="lt-hero">
          <span class="eyebrow">Free Study Type Quiz for Students</span>
          <h1 class="lt-h1">
            What's my study type?<br />You're not studying too little — you're
            studying <span class="hl">in the wrong place</span>.
          </h1>
          <p class="lt-lede">
            Most students don't fail because of a lack of time or discipline —
            they fail at one single point in their own study process, and go
            years without noticing which one. This free quiz shows you, in
            eight questions, where things actually break down for you and
            exactly what fixes it.
          </p>
          <button class="btn lt-btn-block" type="button" onclick="start()">
            Start the free quiz now →
          </button>
          <ul class="lt-meta">
            <li>8 questions</li>
            <li>under 60 seconds</li>
            <li>no login</li>
            <li>free</li>
          </ul>

          <div class="lt-cast" aria-hidden="true">
            <img src="/img/lerntypen/markierer@1x.webp" alt="" width="450" height="670" loading="eager" />
            <img src="/img/lerntypen/koenner@1x.webp" alt="" width="450" height="692" loading="eager" />
            <img src="/img/lerntypen/sprinter@1x.webp" alt="" width="450" height="658" loading="eager" />
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- 2 — Recognition: symptoms to check off -->
        <section class="lt-band">
          <h2 class="rule">Sound familiar?</h2>
          <ul class="lt-symptoms">
            <li>You read a chapter, understand all of it — and two days later it's gone.</li>
            <li>You know the answer. You just can't get it out when someone asks out loud.</li>
            <li>You sit down to study and burn twenty minutes deciding where to even start.</li>
            <li>You've been studying for weeks and still feel like you don't know any of it.</li>
            <li>You plan to do something every day — and nobody notices when you don't.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="lt-turn">
            If any of this sounds familiar: it's rarely laziness behind it.
            What's almost always behind it is that you're pouring a lot of
            energy into a spot where it doesn't pay off.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- 3 — Relief and mechanism -->
        <section class="lt-band">
          <h2 class="rule">Why the usual study tips don't work for you</h2>
          <p>
            You know the classic breakdown into "visual," "auditory," and
            "kinesthetic" learners. It sounds convincing — and it's been
            debunked. Studies find no evidence that material sticks better
            when it matches your preferred sensory channel. Studying that way
            optimizes the wrong lever.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>So it's not you.</strong> It's advice built to apply to
            everyone at once, which means it never quite fits anyone.
            What matters isn't how you prefer to take in information, but
            <strong>where exactly your study process breaks down</strong> —
            gathering material, processing it, recalling it, or sticking with
            it.
          </p>
          <p>
            That's exactly what this quiz measures. And because everyone's
            breaking point sits somewhere different, the fix is different for
            everyone too.
          </p>
          <div class="lt-cta-inline">
            <button class="btn" type="button" onclick="start()">
              Find my breaking point →
            </button>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- 4 — What the quiz gives you -->
        <section class="lt-band">
          <h2 class="rule">What the quiz tells you</h2>
          <div class="lt-benefits">
            <div class="lt-benefit">
              <span class="lt-benefit__num">01</span>
              <h3>Your strength</h3>
              <p>
                What you're actually good at. Every one of the six profiles
                has a real skill at its core — it's just being applied in the
                wrong place.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="lt-benefit">
              <span class="lt-benefit__num">02</span>
              <h3>Your breaking point</h3>
              <p>
                The one spot where your study time evaporates — named,
                explained, and tied to what it's actually costing you on
                exam day.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="lt-benefit">
              <span class="lt-benefit__num">03</span>
              <h3>Your next step</h3>
              <p>
                Not a generic study tip, but the fix that matches your
                profile — in three steps, ready to use right away.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- 5 — Type preview: raises the question "which one am I?" -->
        <section class="lt-band">
          <h2 class="rule">Which type are you?</h2>
          <p class="lt-band__intro">
            Six profiles, six different places where study time goes to
            waste. None of them is a verdict on your intelligence — each one
            describes a habit you can change.
          </p>
          <p class="lt-band__hinweis">
            Looking for the classic learning styles — visual, auditory,
            kinesthetic? We deliberately don't use those.
            <a href="/lerntypen/">Here's why that model doesn't hold up to
            scrutiny</a> and what the research recommends instead. (In
            German for now — an English version is on the way.)
          </p>

          <div class="lt-types">
            <article class="lt-type">
              <img src="/img/lerntypen/koenner@1x.webp" srcset="/img/lerntypen/koenner@1x.webp 450w, /img/lerntypen/koenner.webp 900w" sizes="(max-width: 640px) 40vw, 200px" width="450" height="692" alt="Illustration: student sitting cross-legged, searching for words" loading="lazy" />
              <div>
                <h3>The Quiet Achiever</h3>
                <p class="lt-type__line">"You know it. Until you have to say it."</p>
                <p>
                  Really understands the material and never learns anything
                  by rote. But only ever trains understanding, never free
                  recall — and blanks out the moment it's asked out loud.
                </p>
              </div>
            </article>

            <article class="lt-type">
              <img src="/img/lerntypen/sammler@1x.webp" srcset="/img/lerntypen/sammler@1x.webp 450w, /img/lerntypen/sammler.webp 900w" sizes="(max-width: 640px) 40vw, 200px" width="450" height="595" alt="Illustration: student between tall stacks of paper, arms full of more" loading="lazy" />
              <div>
                <h3>The Collector</h3>
                <p class="lt-type__line">"You have everything. You've learned none of it."</p>
                <p>
                  Has every slide, every handout, every note. Collecting
                  feels like progress, but it keeps pushing the actual work
                  further down the road.
                </p>
              </div>
            </article>

            <article class="lt-type">
              <img src="/img/lerntypen/markierer@1x.webp" srcset="/img/lerntypen/markierer@1x.webp 450w, /img/lerntypen/markierer.webp 900w" sizes="(max-width: 640px) 40vw, 200px" width="450" height="670" alt="Illustration: student highlighting a page that's already fully covered in color" loading="lazy" />
              <div>
                <h3>The Highlighter</h3>
                <p class="lt-type__line">"Colorful doesn't mean learned."</p>
                <p>
                  Hardworking and persistent. But highlighting and rereading
                  create familiarity, not recall — the single best-documented
                  study trap there is.
                </p>
              </div>
            </article>

            <article class="lt-type">
              <img src="/img/lerntypen/ueberfordert@1x.webp" srcset="/img/lerntypen/ueberfordert@1x.webp 450w, /img/lerntypen/ueberfordert.webp 900w" sizes="(max-width: 640px) 40vw, 200px" width="450" height="598" alt="Illustration: student sitting among several open books, hesitating" loading="lazy" />
              <div>
                <h3>The Overwhelmed</h3>
                <p class="lt-type__line">"Not too little time. Too many false starts."</p>
                <p>
                  Not a discipline problem, a decision problem. As long as
                  the whole subject sits there at once, figuring out where to
                  start eats the energy that should go into studying.
                </p>
              </div>
            </article>

            <article class="lt-type">
              <img src="/img/lerntypen/einzel@1x.webp" srcset="/img/lerntypen/einzel@1x.webp 450w, /img/lerntypen/einzel.webp 900w" sizes="(max-width: 640px) 40vw, 200px" width="450" height="438" alt="Illustration: student sitting alone next to an empty folding chair" loading="lazy" />
              <div>
                <h3>The Lone Wolf</h3>
                <p class="lt-type__line">"Nobody notices whether you do it."</p>
                <p>
                  Can work alone and stay focused. What's missing isn't a
                  method, it's accountability — a promise nobody's watching
                  costs nothing when it's broken.
                </p>
              </div>
            </article>

            <article class="lt-type">
              <img src="/img/lerntypen/sprinter@1x.webp" srcset="/img/lerntypen/sprinter@1x.webp 450w, /img/lerntypen/sprinter.webp 900w" sizes="(max-width: 640px) 40vw, 200px" width="450" height="658" alt="Illustration: student running with books and a coffee cup, papers flying behind" loading="lazy" />
              <div>
                <h3>The Sprinter</h3>
                <p class="lt-type__line">"You pull it off. You just don't retain it."</p>
                <p>
                  Performs surprisingly well under pressure. But without
                  reviewing over several days, the material fades — and it
                  catches up with you on the next exam that builds on it.
                </p>
              </div>
            </article>
          </div>

          <div class="lt-cta-inline">
            <button class="btn" type="button" onclick="start()">
              Find out which one I am →
            </button>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- 6 — Evidence instead of authority -->
        <section class="lt-band">
          <h2 class="rule">What the quiz is based on</h2>
          <p>
            The results aren't based on a personality theory, but on learning
            science. Two findings matter most here, and both are confirmed
            across major reviews spanning subjects, age groups, and exam
            formats:
          </p>
          <ul class="lt-evidence">
            <li>
              <strong>Testing yourself beats rereading, by a lot.</strong>
              Rereading feels better right afterward — but clearly worse
              after a few days, and it makes you more confident than you
              actually are.
              <cite>Roediger &amp; Karpicke 2006 · Dunlosky et al. 2013</cite>
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Spaced study beats cramming.</strong>
              The same material spread across several days stays available
              far longer than the same amount crammed into one long session.
              <cite>Dunlosky et al. 2013</cite>
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Highlighting and rereading — the two most popular study methods
            of all — landed in the lowest-effectiveness category in the same
            review. So this quiz isn't testing your preferences. It's testing
            your habits.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- 7 — Closing CTA -->
        <section class="lt-final">
          <h2>Eight questions. Then you'll know.</h2>
          <p>
            No account, no email address, no sharing your answers. The quiz
            runs entirely in your browser.
          </p>
          <button class="btn lt-btn-block" type="button" onclick="start()">
            Start the free quiz now →
          </button>
          <p class="lt-fine">Takes under a minute</p>
        </section>
      </section>


      <!-- ------------------------------------------- Subject (Step 0) -- -->
      <section id="s-fach" class="lt-screen">
        <div class="lt-top">
          <div class="lt-mascot" id="mascot-fach"></div>
          <div class="lt-progress">
            <div class="lt-progress__head">
              <span class="lt-count">Quick heads-up</span>
              <span class="lt-mood">Doesn't count</span>
            </div>
            <div class="lt-track"><span class="lt-fill" style="width:6%"></span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="lt-q">What are you studying?</p>
        <p class="lt-fachhint">
          So the examples match your subject. One answer, then the eight
          questions start.
        </p>
        <div class="lt-faecher" id="faecher"></div>
      </section>

      <!-- ----------------------------------------------------- Quiz -- -->
      <section id="s-quiz" class="lt-screen">
        <div class="lt-top">
          <div class="lt-mascot" id="mascot"></div>
          <div class="lt-progress">
            <div class="lt-progress__head">
              <span class="lt-count" id="count">Question 1 of 8</span>
              <span class="lt-mood" id="mood"></span>
            </div>
            <div class="lt-track"><span class="lt-fill" id="fill"></span></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="lt-q" id="q"></p>
        <div class="lt-opts" id="opts"></div>
        <p class="lt-note" id="note"></p>
        <button class="lt-back hide" id="back" type="button" onclick="back()">
          ← back
        </button>
      </section>

      <!-- -------------------------------------------------- Result -- -->
      <section id="s-result" class="lt-screen lt-result"></section>
      <canvas id="confetti" class="lt-confetti" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>

    <!-- ------------------------------------------------- Android waitlist -- -->
    <div class="lt-overlay hide" id="waitlist" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="wl-title">
      <div class="lt-dialog">
        <button class="lt-dialog__x" type="button" onclick="closeWaitlist()" aria-label="Close">✕</button>
        <h3 id="wl-title">Android version</h3>
        <p>
          Octa is currently iPhone and iPad only. The Android version is in
          the works — sign up and we'll let you know the moment it's ready.
        </p>
        <div id="wl-body"></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    </div>

  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style is:global>
  /* =====================================================================
     Lerntyp-Test — eigene Formsprache, aber auf den Design-Tokens der
     Seite aufgebaut. Bewusst `is:global`, weil ein Teil des Markups zur
     Laufzeit per innerHTML entsteht und Astros Scoping dort nicht greift.
     Alle Klassen sind mit `lt-` praefixiert.
     ===================================================================== */

  .lt-page {
    padding-block: 0 1rem;
  }

  .lt-shell {
    position: relative;
    max-width: 40rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .lt-screen {
    display: none;
  }

  .lt-screen.on {
    display: block;
    animation: lt-rise 0.34s cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.7, 0.3, 1) both;
  }

  @keyframes lt-rise {
    from {
      opacity: 0;
      transform: translateY(12px);
    }
    to {
      opacity: 1;
      transform: none;
    }
  }

  .hide {
    display: none !important;
  }

  /* ------------------------------------------------------------ Intro -- */

  .lt-h1 {
    margin: 0.35rem 0 0.9rem;
  }

  .lt-lede {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    max-width: 34rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .lt-btn-block {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 24rem;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    padding-block: 1rem;
  }

  .lt-meta {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem 1.4rem;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 1.1rem 0 0;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-subtle);
  }

  .lt-meta li {
    margin-top: 0;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.45rem;
  }

  .lt-meta li::before {
    content: '';
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--accent);
    flex: none;
  }

  /* ------------------------------------------------------ Fortschritt -- */

  .lt-top {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .lt-mascot {
    flex: none;
    width: 60px;
    height: 60px;
  }

  .lt-mascot svg {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
  }

  .lt-progress {
    flex: 1;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .lt-progress__head {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .lt-count {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .lt-mood {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--text-subtle);
    text-align: right;
  }

  .lt-track {
    height: 8px;
    background: var(--bg-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .lt-fill {
    display: block;
    height: 100%;
    width: 0;
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    background-image: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--cta-from), var(--accent));
    transition: width 0.45s cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.7, 0.3, 1);
  }

  /* ------------------------------------------------------------ Frage -- */

  .lt-q {
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 1.1rem + 1.4vw, 1.85rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1.25;
    letter-spacing: -0.012em;
    margin-bottom: 1.4rem;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .lt-opts {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.65rem;
  }

  .lt-opt {
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.9rem;
    width: 100%;
    text-align: left;
    cursor: pointer;
    background: var(--bg-card);
    color: var(--text);
    border: 1.5px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 1rem 1.15rem;
    font: inherit;
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
    transition: border-color 0.15s ease, background 0.15s ease,
      transform 0.12s ease, box-shadow 0.15s ease;
  }

  .lt-opt__key {
    flex: none;
    width: 1.75rem;
    height: 1.75rem;
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: var(--bg-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    color: var(--text-subtle);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    transition: background 0.15s ease, color 0.15s ease,
      border-color 0.15s ease;
  }

  .lt-opt:hover {
    border-color: var(--accent);
    transform: translateX(3px);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
  }

  .lt-opt:hover .lt-opt__key {
    background: var(--accent-soft);
    color: var(--accent);
    border-color: transparent;
  }

  .lt-opt.picked {
    border-color: transparent;
    background-image: linear-gradient(100deg, var(--cta-from), var(--cta-to));
    color: #fff;
    transform: scale(0.985);
  }

  .lt-opt.picked .lt-opt__key {
    background: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.22);
    color: #fff;
    border-color: transparent;
  }

  .lt-note {
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
    padding: 0.9rem 1.1rem;
    background: var(--bg-soft);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius) var(--radius) 0;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .lt-note b {
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .lt-note cite {
    font-style: normal;
    color: var(--text-subtle);
  }

  .lt-back {
    background: none;
    border: 0;
    color: var(--text-subtle);
    font: inherit;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    padding: 0.7rem 0;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  .lt-back:hover {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  /* --------------------------------------------------------- Ergebnis -- */

  .lt-result-head {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .lt-result-char {
    margin-inline: auto;
    width: 148px;
    height: 148px;
  }

  .lt-result-char svg {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    animation: lt-pop 0.55s cubic-bezier(0.2, 1.5, 0.4, 1) both;
  }

  @keyframes lt-pop {
    from {
      opacity: 0;
      transform: scale(0.4) rotate(-8deg);
    }
    to {
      opacity: 1;
      transform: none;
    }
  }

  .lt-tagline {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--highlight);
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .lt-befund {
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 2.25rem;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
  }

  .lt-bars {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.85rem;
  }

  .lt-bar-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 4.5rem;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.9rem;
  }

  .lt-bar-name {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
  }

  .lt-bar-row.top-hit .lt-bar-name {
    color: var(--text);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .lt-bar-track {
    height: 8px;
    background: var(--bg-soft);
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .lt-bar-fill {
    display: block;
    height: 100%;
    width: 0;
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    background: var(--border-strong);
    transition: width 0.8s cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.7, 0.3, 1);
  }

  .lt-bar-row.top-hit .lt-bar-fill {
    background-image: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--cta-from), var(--accent));
  }

  .lt-bar-val {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text-subtle);
    text-align: right;
  }

  .lt-block {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .lt-block h3 {
    margin-top: 0;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .lt-moment {
    font-size: 1.08rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--text);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--highlight);
    padding: 0.15rem 0 0.15rem 1.1rem;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .lt-steps {
    list-style: none;
    counter-reset: lt;
    margin: 1.1rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .lt-steps li {
    counter-increment: lt;
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 3rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .lt-steps li::before {
    content: counter(lt);
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.1rem;
    width: 2rem;
    height: 2rem;
    border-radius: 10px;
    background-image: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--cta-from), var(--accent));
    color: #fff;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
  }

  .lt-divider {
    border: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    margin: 2.5rem 0;
  }

  /* Demo-Platzhalter */
  .lt-demo {
    border: 1.5px dashed var(--border-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: 2rem 1.25rem;
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--text-subtle);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    background: var(--bg-soft);
  }

  .lt-demo strong {
    display: block;
    color: var(--text-muted);
